Contract: `lastN(s []int, n int) []int` returns the last n elements of s in original order. If n >= len(s) it returns all of s; if n <= 0 it returns an empty slice. It must never panic. Does this meet the contract?

```go
func lastN(s []int, n int) []int {
    if n <= 0 {
        return []int{}
    }
    return s[len(s)-n:]
}
```
